\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Community totals miss internal overflow at critical fill. Left: 4096 saved endpoints at $q=512$, $\kappa =1$, $\lambda =1$, with matching crosses. The profile curve retains internal variation; $|D|/2$ uses only community excess. Their gap at $D=0$ is approximately $0.6313$. Right: absolute-error distributions for the same endpoints, with mean absolute errors in the legend. Both readouts use the observed imbalance. This is a descriptive mechanism comparison; the separate terminal test checks the diffusion. The frozen profile lookup error is at most $0.000026$.}}{2}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:profileablation}{{1}{2}{Community totals miss internal overflow at critical fill. Left: 4096 saved endpoints at $q=512$, $\kappa =1$, $\lambda =1$, with matching crosses. The profile curve retains internal variation; $|D|/2$ uses only community excess. Their gap at $D=0$ is approximately $0.6313$. Right: absolute-error distributions for the same endpoints, with mean absolute errors in the legend. Both readouts use the observed imbalance. This is a descriptive mechanism comparison; the separate terminal test checks the diffusion. The frozen profile lookup error is at most $0.000026$}{figure.2}{}}
