\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The fixed allocation rule and its critical scales. Each of the four sides contains $m=q/2$ buckets. Internal directions have probability $(1-\varepsilon )/2$ each; cross directions have probability $\varepsilon /2$ each. The offered cross endpoints have uniform marginals under any fixed doubly stochastic kernel. The algorithm increments the smaller endpoint load and chooses the left endpoint at a tie. The limiting diffusion retains community imbalance; the overflow readout also retains the internal profile.}}{4}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:model}{{2}{4}{The fixed allocation rule and its critical scales. Each of the four sides contains $m=q/2$ buckets. Internal directions have probability $(1-\eps )/2$ each; cross directions have probability $\eps /2$ each. The offered cross endpoints have uniform marginals under any fixed doubly stochastic kernel. The algorithm increments the smaller endpoint load and chooses the left endpoint at a tie. The limiting diffusion retains community imbalance; the overflow readout also retains the internal profile}{figure.10}{}}
\newlabel{fig:model@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][3][]4}{}{}{}}
